2... Bb7 3. g3 e6 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. c4 d5 6. O-O
{ Do not rush tactics. Castle, complete development, and then use cxd5 or Ne5 when the center clarifies. }
6... Be7 7. Nc3 ) ( 2. g3 Bb7 3. Bg2 c5
{ If Black plays ...c5 before ...d5, occupy with c4/d4 and recapture toward active piece play. }
4. O-O Nf6 5. c4 e6 6. d4 cxd4 7. Nxd4
{ Nxd4 keeps pieces centralized and avoids giving Black easy dark-square pressure. }
7... Bxg2 8. Kxg2 ) 2... Bb7 3. Bg2 e6 4. O-O
{ Castle first; keep the central pawns flexible until Black shows the structure. }
4... Nf6 5. c4 d5 6. d4
{ Now d4 is useful because it gives you a real center with c4 already restraining d5. }
6... Be7 7. Nc3 O-O 8. cxd5
{ When Black accepts an isolated-pawn or hanging-pawn structure, central squares like e5 become your targets. }
8... exd5 9. Ne5 *

